-- title:
--   A multiple-side box mean splits into quotient and residue means
-- statement:
--   Let the coordinate type be finite with decidable equality, let $q_i,D\in\mathbb N$, and let $F$ be real-valued on natural-coordinate vectors. The box mean with side lengths $q_iD$ equals the iterated normalized mean of $F(r_i+Da_i)$ over $a_i\in\mathrm{Fin}(q_i)$ and $r_i\in\mathrm{Fin}(D)$. No periodicity is assumed.
